backend — local-first, versioned code intelligence

Usage: backend [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [OPERANDS]

library
  packages                                List every package on the shelf with its status and declaration counts.
  add [PATH] [--execution-intent INTENT]  Index a local project directory, or refresh its existing indexed contents.
  remove <PATH>                           Remove one package and its derived indexes from the shelf.
  show <COORDINATE>                       Render one declaration page: signature, documentation, members, relations, and source.
  source <COORDINATE>                     Read the source text of one declaration with a few lines of context either side.
  related <COORDINATE>                    List the symbols related to one declaration through its links, its siblings, and the vector space.
  references <COORDINATE>                 List the places one declaration is used, with the exact source span that proves each use.
  read <COORDINATE>...                    Render several declaration pages in one call, each answered or refused on its own.
  diff <PACKAGE> <PACKAGE>                Compare two versions of one package: declarations added, removed, and changed in signature.
  outline [PATH]                          Render one package's containment tree.
  resolve <TEXT> [--limit COUNT] [--cursor CURSOR]  Turn a readable address into exact declarations, reporting ambiguity instead of guessing.
  search <TEXT> [--limit COUNT] [--cursor CURSOR]  Search exact keys, names, relations, and vectors together; every lane reports its coverage.
  graph <COORDINATE>                      Traverse calls, implementations, references, and other relations from one declaration.
  semantic-versions <PACKAGE>             List immutable compiler generations retained for one exact package.
  semantic-shapes <SHAPE_REQUEST_JSON>    Read bounded compiler-owned callable and member shapes for selected declarations.
  package-source-membership <MEMBERSHIP_REQUEST_JSON>  Read a bounded, snapshot-bound page of exact File rows selected by one local Project, including package-relative paths and source identities.
  select-semantic-version <PACKAGE> <PURL> <PROFILE> <GENERATION>  Select one exact retained compiler generation for local product projection.
  cargo-source-file <SOURCE_REQUEST_JSON> <TEXT>  Read one bounded source or documentation file using the exact Cargo package authority and ProjectTree root binding currently observed by the owner.
  cargo-source-inventory <SOURCE_REQUEST_JSON>  List a bounded set of currently observed source and documentation paths under one exact Cargo package authority and ProjectTree root binding.
  cargo-package-readme <PACKAGE>          Read the bounded README Cargo selects from one exact package release's observed manifest and source authority.
  cargo-package-readme-link <ORIGIN_JSON> <TEXT>  Read one bounded relative link from a current owner-admitted package README under its exact package or workspace root.
  index_start <PACKAGE> [--execution-intent INTENT]  Start one package indexing job and return its owner-issued ticket.
  index_await <TICKET>                    Wait for the terminal receipt of one owner-issued package indexing job.
  index_cancel <TICKET>                   Request cancellation of one exact owner-issued package indexing job.
  index_progress <TICKET> [--after-sequence SEQUENCE]  Read the next bounded page of typed progress facts for one owner-issued package indexing job.

registry
  advisory <PACKAGE> [--override-actor TEXT] [--override-reason TEXT] [--override-policy-version TEXT] [--override-expires-at TEXT]  Show advisory sources, affected ranges, freshness, coverage, and the acquisition decision for one package version.
  explore [TEXT] [--limit COUNT]          Browse or search the package registries across every ecosystem, sorted and paged.
  package <PACKAGE>                       Show one registry package: readme, versions, owners, dependencies, dependents, downloads, and how to install it.
  dependents <PACKAGE>                    List the packages that depend on one registry package, most downloaded first.
  dependencies <PACKAGE>                  List the packages one registry package declares, preserving requirements and scopes.
  owner <TEXT>                            List every package one owner publishes, across ecosystems.
  index-search <TEXT> [--limit COUNT] [--cursor CURSOR]  Search every package the local registry index knows by name prefix and term.
  package-versions <PACKAGE>              List every version of one package the index recorded, with checksum and yanked state.
  package-profile <PACKAGE>               Show one package's latest version and full version history from the index.
  forge-add <FORGE>                       Acquire a pinned GitHub, GitLab, Codeberg, or HTTPS Git source and discover its package manifests.
  forge-reference <FORGE>                 Read an exact code-forge source already present in the local content-addressed cache.
  package-graph <PACKAGE> <DIRECTION> [--authority TEXT] [--limit COUNT] [--cursor CURSOR]  Read one bounded page of a package's dependencies or dependents, preserving the exact source authority, ecosystem, version requirement, resolver scope, and graph snapshot.

home
  subscribe <PACKAGE> [--project PROJECT]  Follow one package for new releases, optionally filing it into a project folder.
  unsubscribe <PACKAGE>                   Stop following one package.
  subscriptions                           List every followed package with how many releases you have not seen.
  releases [--mark-seen]                  List new versions of followed packages since you last looked, optionally marking them seen.
  projects                                List every project folder with its members and lockfile binding.
  project-create <NAME> [--lockfile LOCKFILE]  Create a project folder, optionally bound to a lockfile it stays in sync with.
  project-delete <PROJECT>                Delete a project folder; its subscriptions are kept.
  project-add <PROJECT> <PACKAGE>         Put one pinned package into a project folder.
  project-remove <PROJECT> <PACKAGE>      Take one package out of a project folder.
  project-sync <PROJECT>                  Reconcile a project folder with its lockfile, optionally compiling members not yet on the shelf.
  project-tree [PATH]                     Read a project's dependency tree as Cargo resolves it here: the role each dependency plays, why every package is in the tree, which are here twice, and what the advisory sources say.

session
  tree                                    Show the tree of every subject opened from any surface, nested under what it was opened from.
  tree-open <SUBJECT> <TEXT> [--parent NODE] [--title TEXT]  Open a package, page, registry entry, owner, gallery, or search in the session tree under a parent node.
  tree-close <NODE> [--branch]            Close one session tree node, or a whole branch.

system
  health                                  Report every capability as ready, unreachable, unconfigured, or detached.
  advisory-refresh                        Refresh the configured RustSec, OSV, and GHSA sources and keep what they say for tree and package reads.

escape hatch
  surface <JSON>                          Execute any tagged SurfaceCommand object verbatim.

options
  --format human|markdown|json  Choose the rendering; markdown matches the MCP text block.
  --json                        Shorthand for --format json.
  --no-color                    Never paint; NO_COLOR and a non-terminal stdout do the same.
  --limit COUNT                 Bound any command that pages.
  --detail LEVEL                JSON projection: summary, standard, or full.
  --project PATH                Select the project; defaults to the current directory.
  --workspace PATH              Select durable state; defaults to this project's private app-data root.
  --endpoint PATH               Connect to a specific local daemon.
  --passive                     With health/status, connect without starting locald or creating state.
  -h, --help                    Show this help, or one command's help after its name.
  -V, --version                 Show the version.

COLUMNS is honoured for width. Exit codes: 0 success, 2 the engine refused,
64 the arguments were wrong, 1 the local endpoint failed.

